# ============================================================
# ~/.claude .gitignore — FAIL-CLOSED (default-deny).
# Ignore everything; explicitly opt in ONLY versionable machinery.
# Rationale: this dir mixes secrets (.credentials.json), confidential
# deal terms (hooks/confidential-terms.json) and transient runtime
# state with the config worth tracking. Default-deny prevents an
# accidental secret commit — matches the firm's fail-closed doctrine.
# To track a new machinery dir, add an explicit "!/<dir>/" line.
# ============================================================

# 1) Ignore everything at root by default (matches dotfiles too)
/*

# 2) Opt IN the machinery worth versioning
!/.gitignore
!/CLAUDE.md
!/settings.json
!/keybindings.json
!/confidential-repos.json
!/uuid-baseline.json
!/check-uuid-drift.sh
!/daily-setup-audit-prompt.md
!/scheduled-tasks-starter-pack.md
!/hooks/
!/commands/
!/agents/
!/skills/
!/maintenance/
!/docs/
!/ora-ops-plugin/
!/.github/

# 2b) Scheduled-task SPECS (SKILL.md only) — versioned 2026-07-12 for durability.
#     Previously unversioned runtime state (repeated loss→restore incidents).
#     ONLY SKILL.md is tracked; runtime state (_state/ _unsent/ logs .bak) stays ignored.
!/scheduled-tasks/
/scheduled-tasks/*
!/scheduled-tasks/*/
/scheduled-tasks/*/*
!/scheduled-tasks/*/SKILL.md
# HOLD — specs referencing a still-listed confidential-roster term (E. Fulton) stay OUT
# until confidential-terms.json is cleaned per rules.md §7b (declassification checklist).
# Re-include these four by deleting their lines once the roster no longer lists the term.
/scheduled-tasks/ora-health-guard/SKILL.md
/scheduled-tasks/ora-open-sessions-board/SKILL.md
/scheduled-tasks/ora-pm-ledger/SKILL.md
/scheduled-tasks/ora-weekly-hygiene/SKILL.md

# 3) Re-ignore secrets, caches & transient state INSIDE opted-in dirs
hooks/confidential-terms.json
hooks/sessions/
# roster-staleness runtime breadcrumb written by confidentiality-guard.py (transient; never track)
hooks/state/
# county-parcel-screen code is TRACKED (counterparty names externalized 2026-06-11);
# its data/ tree (public county dumps + the pipeline-guard.local.json counterparty
# floor) stays local-only. *.local.json is the standing convention for
# never-track local data files anywhere in the repo.
skills/county-parcel-screen/data/
*.local.json
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
*.bak
*.bak-*
